# Pitch decks

This repo publishes one folder per client from `main` to `https://project.np.design/{slug}/`. Layout, spacing, type sizes, and navigation live in `template/` and stay frozen.

The copy, colour roles, palette steps, and QA checklist are in `docs/pitch-playbook.md`.

For a new or updated pitch:

- Start from the template. Copy an existing deck's `pitch.json` shape, or run `node scripts/new-pitch.js <client> --light #RRGGBB --dark #RRGGBB --ink #RRGGBB --accent #RRGGBB`.
- Edit `{slug}/pitch.json` and files in `{slug}/assets/` only.
- Keep the eight slides in order: cover, overview, cards, list, list, process, cost, closing. Rows and cards inside a slide can be longer or shorter.
- Put colours and fonts in `theme`. Generate a palette with `node scripts/pitch-palette.js`. Do not change spacing or type sizes.
- Check with `node scripts/check-pitch.js {slug}` before rebuilding.
- Optional `password` adds a visual gate. Optional `noindex: true` adds a noindex tag. Omit both to leave a deck open and indexable.
- Rebuild with `node scripts/build-pitch.js {slug}`.
- Do not hand-edit `{slug}/index.html`.
- Commit `{slug}/pitch.json`, `{slug}/assets/`, and the generated `{slug}/index.html`, then push `main`, only when asked to publish.

Change `template/` only when the user explicitly asks to change the deck system. See `desa-alam/pitch.json` and `template/pitch.schema.json`.
